I deleted my Instagram account after one day in March, while riding a bicycle down the river, it hit me. What a disgusting space it was. How completely at odds with my values.

Partially, it was about what it did to me. How my thumb knew to find the icon seemingly by itself. How I felt powerless to resist. How angry it made me with myself.

And then the realization that I was creating content for it, so my friends would feel the same. And I felt deeply that I don't want it anymore.

Then my head stepped in and asked: "But what about all the beautiful things?" Surely, there are plenty of beautiful things never to be discovered by me now. It's not about the content. It's about the monstrous machinery the beautiful things live in. Like a flower arrangement in a slaughterhouse.

In this slaughterhouse, you are the meat and the engineers don't really care about beauty.

